From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 22:19:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jsonrpc: also emit an OpenRPC document (openrpc_outdir)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The crate already enables yerpc's `openrpc` feature and every API type
already derives `schemars::JsonSchema`, so the OpenRPC generator is
compiled in and fully fed — it was simply never switched on: `#[rpc]`
sets `ts_outdir` but not `openrpc_outdir`, and without the latter
yerpc_derive emits no OpenRPC generator at all.

Setting it makes `cargo test -p deltachat-jsonrpc` write
`typescript/generated/openrpc.json` next to the TypeScript bindings it
already writes there, from the same `#[rpc]` impl block and the same doc
comments. 177 methods, 40 component schemas. `generated/` is already
gitignored, so nothing new lands in the tree.

This gives non-TypeScript consumers a machine-readable description of
the JSON-RPC API that is generated from the source of truth rather than
transcribed from it.

Since v2.64.0 (yerpc 0.7, #8350) the bindings are generated by the build
script of the new deltachat-jsonrpc-bindings crate and #[rpc] has no
outdir options any more; yerpc 0.7 always generates
RpcServer::openrpc_specification() with the openrpc feature. So the
build script now also writes it to typescript/generated/openrpc.json,
and deltachat-jsonrpc itself is untouched. Run `cargo build -p
deltachat-jsonrpc-bindings` instead of `cargo test -p
deltachat-jsonrpc`.
---
 deltachat-jsonrpc-bindings/build.rs | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deltachat-jsonrpc-bindings/build.rs b/deltachat-jsonrpc-bindings/build.rs
index 744a97fec070219174862568bc4427881fa1cdbb..d6c216231bdebdc27a6dc6a85ed64df05bf6776c 100644
--- a/deltachat-jsonrpc-bindings/build.rs
+++ b/deltachat-jsonrpc-bindings/build.rs
@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@
-use deltachat_jsonrpc::api::{write_qt_bindings, write_ts_bindings};
+use deltachat_jsonrpc::api::{CommandApi, write_qt_bindings, write_ts_bindings};
+use deltachat_jsonrpc::yerpc::RpcServer;
 use std::path::Path;
 
 fn main() {
     write_ts_bindings(Path::new("typescript/generated"));
     write_qt_bindings(Path::new("qt/generated"), "deltachat");
+    // The OpenRPC document of the same API, next to the TypeScript bindings.
+    let openrpc = CommandApi::openrpc_specification().expect("Failed to generate OpenRPC");
+    std::fs::write("typescript/generated/openrpc.json", openrpc).expect("Failed to write OpenRPC");
 }
